1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,882
We'll be arriving at Branley Castle in about five minutes,

2
00:00:04,882 --> 00:00:10,080
but before we get there I'll give you a little information about the castle

3
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:13,020
and what our visit will include.

4
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:18,970
So in fact there's been a castle on this site for over eleven hundred years.

5
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:28,397
The first building was a fort constructed in 914 AD for defence against Danish invaders by King Alfred the Great's daughter,

6
00:00:28,397 --> 00:00:31,090
who ruled England at the time.

7
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:34,384
In the following century, after the Normans conquered England,

8
00:00:34,384 --> 00:00:38,411
the land was given to a nobleman called Richard de Vere,

9
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:45,000
and he built a castle there that stayed in the de Vere family for over four hundred years.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,299
However, when Queen Elizabeth I announced that she was going to visit the castle in 1576,

11
00:00:50,299 --> 00:00:53,480
it was beginning to look a bit run down

12
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:56,922
and it was decided that rather than repair the guest rooms,

13
00:00:56,922 --> 00:01:01,890
they'd make a new house for her out of wood next to the main hall.

14
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:06,899
She stayed there for four nights and apparently it was very luxurious,

15
00:01:06,899 --> 00:01:11,490
but unfortunately it was destroyed a few years later by fire.

16
00:01:11,490 --> 00:01:16,950
In the seventeenth century the castle belonged to the wealthy Fenys family,

17
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:20,590
who enlarged it and made it more comfortable.

18
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:25,837
However, by 1982 the Fenys family could no longer afford to maintain the castle,

19
00:01:25,837 --> 00:01:30,710
even though they received government support, and they put it on the market.

20
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:35,459
It was eventually taken over by a company who owned a number of amusement parks,

21
00:01:35,459 --> 00:01:41,790
but when we get there I think you'll see that they've managed to retain the original atmosphere of the castle.

22
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:52,036
When you go inside, you'll find that in the state rooms there are life-like moving wax models dressed in costumes of different periods in the past,

23
00:01:52,036 --> 00:01:54,400
which even carry on conversations together.

24
00:01:54,400 --> 00:02:01,568
As well as that, in every room there are booklets giving information about what the room was used for

25
00:02:01,568 --> 00:02:05,340
and the history of the objects and furniture it contains.

26
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:10,466
The castle parks quite extensive. At one time sheep were kept there,

27
00:02:10,466 --> 00:02:16,140
and in the nineteenth century the owners had a little zoo with animals like rabbits

28
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:19,010
and even a baby elephant.

29
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:25,570
Nowadays the old zoo buildings are used for public displays of paintings and sculpture.

30
00:02:25,570 --> 00:02:29,195
The park also has some beautiful trees,

31
00:02:29,195 --> 00:02:37,480
though the oldest of all, which dated back 800 years, was sadly blown down in 1987.

32
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:41,657
Now, you're free to wander around on your own until 4:30,

33
00:02:41,657 --> 00:02:48,270
but then at the end of our visit we'll all meet together at the bottom of the Great Staircase.

34
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:50,800
We'll then go on to the long gallery

35
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:54,289
where there's a wonderful collection of photographs showing the family

36
00:02:54,289 --> 00:02:57,633
who owned the castle a hundred years ago having tea

37
00:02:57,633 --> 00:02:58,980
and cakes in the conservatory

38
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:04,990
and we'll then take you to the same place where afternoon tea will be served to you.

39
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:12,036
Now if you can take a look at your plans you'll see Branley Castle has four towers,

40
00:03:12,036 --> 00:03:17,010
joined together by a high wall, with the river on two sides.

41
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:22,798
Don't miss seeing the Great Hall. That's near the river in the main tower,

42
00:03:22,798 --> 00:03:27,760
the biggest one, which was extended and redesigned in the eighteenth century.

43
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:33,200
If you want to get a good view of the whole castle, you can walk around the walls.

44
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:36,237
The starting point's quite near the main entrance -

45
00:03:36,237 --> 00:03:42,310
walk straight down the path until you get to the south gate, and it's just there.

46
00:03:42,310 --> 00:03:47,030
Don't go on to the north gate - there's no way up from there.

47
00:03:47,030 --> 00:03:49,780
There'll shortly be a show in

48
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:55,000
which you can see archers displaying their skill with a bow and arrow.

49
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,581
The quickest way to get there is to take the first left after the main entrance

50
00:04:00,581 --> 00:04:06,860
and follow the path past the bridge, then you'll see it in front of you at the end.

51
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:11,640
If you like animals there's also a display of hunting birds

52
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:15,050
falcons and eagles and so on.

53
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:19,837
If you go from the main entrance in the direction of the south gate,

54
00:04:19,837 --> 00:04:23,941
but turn right before you get there instead of going through it,

55
00:04:23,941 --> 00:04:27,360
you'll see it on your right past the first tower.

56
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:34,480
At 3 pm there's a short performance of traditional dancing on the outdoor stage.

57
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:40,370
That's right at the other side of the castle from the entrance, and over the bridge.

58
00:04:40,370 --> 00:04:43,120
It's about ten minutes' walk or so.

59
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:48,960
And finally the shop. It's actually inside one of the towers

60
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,480
but the way in is from the outside.

61
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:55,720
Just take the first left after the main entrance

62
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:59,601
go down the path and take the first right.

63
00:04:59,601 --> 00:05:02,370
It's got some lovely gifts and souvenirs.

64
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:06,880
Right, so we're just arriving...
